  "description": "Front T1 Sycamore x 1 (Acer pseudoplatanus) This 8m mature sycamore is located close to the front of the property. There are concerns over the proximity of the roots to the front wall. The crown vitality is poor and the lateral growth touches the guttering. Suggested work:- fell to ground level and poison stump to prevent regrowth. Client is willing to replant. Front S1 Sycamore x 1 (Acer pseudoplatanus) Grind down stump to approx. 300mm below ground level Front P1 Photina spp x 1 Plant Photinia Red Robin Multi Stem Parachute 50 Litre Pot 150/160cm Rear T2 False Acacia x 1 (Robinia pseudoacacia) This 14m mature robinia has been reduced previously but not for several years. The tree has outgrown its location and is encroaching upon the garden area. Suggested work: - crown reduction - reduce the height 3m back to previous reduction points - reduce the lateral growth 2m leaving furnishing growth - remove creeper down to crown break",
